# Host window size

`resized()` lays out the bounds the VST3 or CLAP wrapper set. The constructor's `setSize(1200, 580)` is the logical size those wrappers report. It is 1200 by 580 because a 1536x864 screen at 125% scaling has to hold the editor plus the standalone's chrome; the window stays resizable from 1080x540.

Do not call `setSize` from `parentSizeChanged`, `visibilityChanged`, or `parentHierarchyChanged` to match the host window.

`parentHierarchyChanged` may fit the standalone window to the screen once. That is the only editor-initiated size change after construction.
